Out-of-sample comparison

Very few situations in reality where GLMs (with a linear predictor) perform better than an additive model using smooth functions



Especially since smooth functions can just capture linear models


hr_preds |&gt; 
  pivot_longer(cols = gam_pred:logit_pred, 
               names_to = "model", 
               values_to = "test_pred") |&gt; 
  mutate(test_pred_class = round(test_pred)) |&gt; 
  group_by(model, test_fold) |&gt;
  summarize(accuracy = mean(test_pred_class == test_actual)) |&gt; 
  group_by(model) |&gt; 
  summarize(cv_accuracy = mean(accuracy),
            se_accuracy = sd(accuracy) / sqrt(N_FOLDS))

